.TH CLRUCACHE_CAPACITY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
clrucache_capacity \- return the maximum capacity of the cache
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <clrucache.h>

size_t clrucache_capacity(clru_cache cache);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the maximum number of live entries the cache can hold before
eviction begins. This is the value supplied as capacity to
clrucache_create_full() at construction time.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cache  Cache handle.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Capacity (always >= 1 for a valid handle), or 0 if cache is NULL.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Does not acquire the mutex; capacity is immutable after construction.
O(1) complexity.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clrucache_size (3),
.BR clrucache_create_full (3)
